  "hypothesis_statement": "After the merged MV2 wiring_mod capture-alias open_side binding fix, a causally executable, side-aware Bollinger middle-band mean-reversion exit applied after unchanged baseline entries produces a measurable baseline-vs-treatment exit-decision divergence on the sealed DEVELOPMENT_ONLY panel and improves net economics versus the immutable stop-dominated baseline exit path, without changing entry eligibility, direction/side selection, instrument selection, sizing, risk, execution, or canonical 1.0x costs.",
  "scientific_hypothesis": "On the sealed DEVELOPMENT_ONLY Bollinger/MR baseline, material EXIT_LEAKAGE arises because open positions often hold past mean-reversion and exit via stop_loss after giving back favorable excursion. With open_side correctly bound at the MV2 bar-loop capture alias, enforcing a deterministic side-aware middle-band exit at finalized PT1H bars improves exit observability (exit_bars_observed>0) and net economics versus the identical control chain. V4 consumed its one-shot slot and terminated as INFRASTRUCTURE_FAILURE (PROCESS_DIED_INCOMPLETE_PANEL_RUN_NO_LIFECYCLE_TERMINAL) without economic closeout; V5 preserves the identical economic hypothesis/exit mechanism/measurement-validity gates and adds generic process-lifecycle observability with monotonic lifecycle states, atomic checkpoints, and read-only recovery diagnostics so a future authorized run can distinguish active progress, deterministic failure, external process death, incomplete member execution, and lifecycle-terminal completion. V5 fail-closes incomplete/dead runs as INFRASTRUCTURE_FAILURE; partial metrics remain non-authoritative; checkpoints never authorize automatic rerun or a second run slot.",
  "economic_hypothesis": "Relative to the immutable bollinger_bands/v2 canonical baseline on the sealed DEVELOPMENT_ONLY panel at frozen 1.0x costs, and only after measurement-validity gates pass (effective config digests differ; open_side binding observed; exit_bars_observed>0; synthetic divergence observed), the treatment yields jointly: net_return_after_costs_treatment not degraded beyond canonical tolerance vs control, profit_factor_treatment not degraded beyond canonical tolerance vs control, max_drawdown_treatment not worsened beyond canonical tolerance vs control, with cost assumptions remaining fully active.",
  "primary_decision_metric": "NET_RETURN_AFTER_COSTS",
  "primary_decision_metric_contract": "PASS requires measurement-validity gates first (effective configs differ; open_side binding observed; exit_bars_observed>0; synthetic divergence observed), then joint satisfaction of all pass_requires_all economic checks; NET_RETURN_AFTER_COSTS is the lead economic decision metric with profit_factor, max_drawdown, trade/exit counts, holding bars, turnover, and fee/slippage drag as hard companions.",
  "dataset_id": "pit_okx_linear_usdt_non_bitcoin_cross_sectional_pt1h_dev_pre_holdout_v1",
